 "report": "Particle A42-spiral-e000-d018: inhibitory cascade (k=6)\n\nWhat it is: a particle of mass 2.1 and radius 1.52 with 6 ports on its rim. Each port is a stick-slip contact with a dead zone (mean 0.46) and a 4-dim charge; 7 of its port pairs attract each other strongly (so copies can bind port to port). Inside, 12 couplings (67% inhibitory) pass a push from port to port; it settles in 3 sweeps with slip rate 0.99 and keeps its state (memory).\nHow it assembles (32 copies, 2 worlds): 1.19 bonds per particle, largest molecule 6.0 particles, 7.5 left free.\n\nIts matter vs an ESN of the same size (readout only, both with tuned input scale); controls: no bonds, random bonds:\n  memcap   0.078 vs ESN 0.999\u00b10.000  [below]  no bonds 0.073  random bonds 0.082\n  xor      0.546 vs ESN 0.529\u00b10.011  [beat, at chance]  no bonds 0.546  random bonds 0.546\n  narma10  0.187 vs ESN 0.841\u00b10.002  [below]  no bonds 0.201  random bonds 0.238\n  latch    0.933 vs ESN 0.679\u00b10.009  [beat]  no bonds 0.921  random bonds 0.921\n  mnist14  0.507 vs ESN 0.816\u00b10.007  [below]  no bonds 0.478  random bonds 0.498\n\nGood at: latch.\nIts assembly matters on latch: the bonds its copies chose beat both no bonds and random bonds.\nUse (a guess): holding a value until it is overwritten, with nothing trained but the readout: a physical memory element for a recurrent or reservoir system."
